  "notes": "{左折|させつ} is the formal/technical term for turning left, commonly used in traffic contexts and directions.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {左折|させつ}⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧: to turn left\n- {左折|させつ}⟦{禁止|きんし}→禁止：02643_kinshi⟧: no left turn\n- {左折|させつ}⟦{車線|しゃせん}→車線：18949_shasen⟧: left turn lane\n- {左折|させつ}⟦{専用|せんよう}→専用：12385_senyou⟧: left turn only\n\nTRAFFIC NOTES:\n- In Japan, driving is on the left, so {左折|させつ} is similar to right turns in countries with right-side driving\n- Watch for {巻|ま}き⟦{込|こ}み→込み：28615_komi⟧ (cyclists/pedestrians in blind spot)",
